      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-12T15:46:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`data-\u003einfo` is the cached chip info that we seed during INIT and refresh each time a user calls get_ic_status; it isn\u0027t temporary.\n\nWe do write directly to `data-\u003einfo` when calling `cmd_get_ic_status_sync_internal()` from the init state, and when called by users we write directly to the user-supplied buffer and also store a copy into `data-\u003einfo` so the driver can have it retained for a subsequent non-live read.",
      "parentUuid": "2bb7254c_e6f01746",
      "revId": "de0ec4393e9418248c1021ce32a5128ecfdfdf93",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
